  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Return and Reintegration: Essential Actions for the Construction of Peace in El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project recognizes the importance of comprehensive care for the reintegration of returnees and displacement affected populations, with emphasis on the situation of girls and boys in El Salvador. The initiative seeks results through addressing different economic and psychosocial aspects of care for the returned and displaced migrant population of various profiles. Efforts are directed at strengthening institutional mechanisms to ensure the sustainability and continuity of actions. In each of these results, the areas of prevention, protection and reintegration are linked through productive and economic dynamization, promoting inter-agency work to achieve joint results.</narrative>
  </description>
